how working practices are going to change, both outwardly to the Ds and Court etc, and whether a working group should be set up to standardise approach e.g. do all things on
 the PG SharePoint move across to LD - what is the timeframe, how is it co-ordinated? Whilst an administrative concern this does have significance in terms of sheer volume and also maintaining/transferring admin rights for links particularly where the Defendants
 and the Court already retain access.&nbsp;




How does it work for the costs team?&nbsp;

&nbsp;
Each of these, along with sight of the AA, will go some way to helping the PG staff understand the agreement they are
 now working under and hopefully to stop the wheels from falling off. This will also assist in answering questions the Case Leads have, but it will not, we doubt, satisfy any regulatory concerns we have, and we request again the Board's complete answer to our
 note of 05.10.2025 (under cover of email of Sarah Bingham). To date we have not had any answer from you.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
On this point, we thought it helpful to also compile a few outstanding requests from our end to you / the Board.
We should also say thank you again for speaking to Alicia and arranging the call with the employment solicitor. While we hope this will assist in clarifying the position in terms of whether this AA can be
 imposed upon us and not contravene our employment contracts, it will not be able to answer any of our regulatory concerns (in respect of the AA and wider regulatory concerns). These really can only be answered by the following:&nbsp;
&nbsp;



the advice from BWKC or any other counsel on the AA. This is especially true where many of the concerns we have raised overlap with those in the HSFK letter - including the regulatory
 position for us as lawyers, and the position on client consent. We still have not consented to the AA and we all have significant regulatory concerns. In particular we have not seen any advice which contradicts our position that client consent is necessary
 for the AA.




Re the AA and how strategic decisions are made, a very practical question: in circumstances where LD and PG (either collaboratively or by PG being informed) make a decision,
 do the PG bods have to in turn report these to the Board / AV? Do we have to report where decisions have been made that we do not agree with? What is our internal reporting matrix for issues such as this?&nbsp;




Will our COLP, in their role as COLP, be giving us sign off on the agreement, in addition to the Counsel advice?




As our COLP is now also a case lead (for Pan NOx and it appears individual cases), is there a delineation of the COLP roles, from the role of case lead, and CEO of the firm?
 How is this safeguarded?

&nbsp;
If these questions are not answered to a satisfactory standard, then our regulatory concerns will remain and as regulated
 persons, we will need to consider our positions and what, if any, further steps we need to take.
&nbsp;
Thanks,
