&nbsp;
Summary of Key points discussed:
&nbsp;

Timing of Service
PG will confirm that the application will not be served today; anticipated service is on before Thursday (Thursday
 latest).Sent letter.


&nbsp;

Format of Statement of Costs
[Agreed]
Final version to be served as a PDF with annexes and an overall summary section, not as a spreadsheet.Soft copy and hard copy will be circulated for review before final version so we can see how it is laid out.


&nbsp;

Profit Costs &amp; Figures
Current profit costs summary shows significant figures (approx. £36m for Sept 2018–Aug 2022), excluding jurisdiction
 costs (£24m).Jurisdiction costs and bill of costs prepared previously should be referenced in the witness statement for context.
[Yes – I’ll do that when I review the draft WS]Consider including a short summary of the bill of costs to demonstrate proper work has been done.
[I don’t think that we’ll need to exhibit any summary – I’ll just insert appropriate wording in the WS]


&nbsp;

Chronology &amp; Narrative
[Agreed]
Court will expect a clear link between monthly costs and work streams.Chronology provided by Sarah is a good starting point; needs more substance to explain intensive periods (e.g., Jan–July
 2019 APOCs, walk-in centres, expert evidence).Suggestion: Use high-level descriptions per month rather than individual fee earner detail.


&nbsp;

Fee Earner Data
[Agreed]
Current list includes 1,093 fee earners; this needs rationalization.Proposal: Split into categories – UK lawyers, foreign lawyers, and walk-in centre staff.Grade D fee earners (approx. £90m, 480,000 hours) to be grouped and summarized rather than listed individually to reduce
 complexity. [Those belonging to the UK lawyers and foreign lawyers sub-categories will be identified in those sections of the Statement (unless this would result in too
 many names) – in any event, there is no need to identify the walk-in centre staff]


&nbsp;

Counsel Fees &amp; Disbursements
[Agreed]
Counsel fees confirmed as correct.Disbursements: Add short descriptions for major items (e.g., expert advice, trial bundles) for clarity.Latham &amp; Watkins and WMC entries require careful wording to explain their role.


&nbsp;

Interest Calculation
Cannot be completed today; will be addressed in due course.
[No need for detailed calculation – I will suggest an appropriate rate and period(s) for interest on costs in the supporting WS]


&nbsp;

Presentation &amp; Witness Statement
[Agreed]
Witness statement to clarify what is included/excluded, basis of recoverability, and provide narrative for Grade D
 costs and walk-in centre work.Make clear that listed costs are conservative and understate actual expenditure.


&nbsp;

&nbsp;
Action List
&nbsp;



&nbsp;
Split Grade D fee earners into UK, Brazilian, and walk-in centre categories – so we then have 3 Fee Earner Sub sections (1. UK Lawyers 2. Foreign Lawyers 3. Walk in Centres &amp; identify them clearly)
Dougie to help Francis and Ben in separating the Grade D Earners into the 3 subsections and outlining what they did briefly.


&nbsp;



Add short descriptions to major disbursements
PG Team to draft concise explanations for key items (e.g., expert advice, trial bundles, Latham &amp; Watkins, WMC – such as assistance in connection with trial preparation to counsel and PG ).



&nbsp;



Circulate updated PDF version of statement of costs with annexes
Ben and Francis to prepare and share for review



&nbsp;



Expand chronology with more substance for key periods
Sarah &amp; PG Team to expand chronology for intensive work phases, main fee earners and link to Profit costs monthly breakdown, use the narrative already drafted internally to help. Plus flesh out the pre-action stage where possible.



&nbsp;



Prepare narrative for Grade D costs and walk-in centre work
Sarah and PG Team to draft explanatory text for inclusion in witness statement (e.g. the amount of POCs &amp; APOCs)
&nbsp;and chronology – need to explain what was done and where.



&nbsp;



Confirm whether bill of costs summary can be used and share with PG for approval
Francis/Ben to liaise with PG and circulate summary if approved.



&nbsp;

&nbsp;



Draft witness statement incorporating disclaimers and narrative



1.&nbsp;Need to explain that we have excluded costs, only have ones which we believe are recoverable (there is also clarity of this in the disclaimers).

2.&nbsp;We are reducing the number of Barristers to the top 10 (95% of costs still) but need to state in the Witness Statement that these are understatements of the actual costs.

3.&nbsp;Basis of grade D earners work – claiming 90 million so need to justify the cost.
