 of the ATE Insurance Policies or ii.) sums already paid under clause 2 or 3 of this Agreement.2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Where the Law Firm receives Law Firm Success Fees and no Claims have been paid by Insurers, or the Claims paid by Insurers do not exhaust the Insurer Proceeds, and the Insurers subsequently pay any Claim, then within five business days of the Insurer’s payment of the Claim, the Law Firm shall pay the Insurers, up to the Insurer Proceeds, or remaining Insurer Proceeds, as the case may be, an amount equal to 50% of the aggregate amounts paid by the Insurers less any Claims that: i.) have been repaid pursuant to clause 3 of the Priorities Deeds that relate to each of the ATE Insurance Policies or ii.) sums already paid under clause 2 or 3 of this Agreement.3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The Law Firm shall make any payments required under this Clause 2 into the Insurer Distribution Account for distribution between the Insurers on a pro rata and pari passu basis in accordance with the total amount paid by the Insurers as at the Assessment Date. Payment to the Insurers from the Insurer Distribution Account shall be made in accordance with Clause 5. The obligations of the Law Firm under this Clause 2 are referred to herein as the “Obligation”.&nbsp;&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;James Burke&nbsp;Associate Director (Solicitor)FINEX Global&nbsp;WTWOn behalf of Willis Limited, 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ (registered number 181116)On behalf of Willis Towers Watson SA/NV, Quai des Vennes, 4020, Liège, Belgium (registered as a branch in the UK at 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ UK Branch Number BR021056) in relation to all EEA-regulated business&nbsp;D: +44 (0)20 31248037M: +44 (0)7831 162591&nbsp;james.burke2@wtwco.comwww.wtwco.com&nbsp;Financial, Professional, and Executive Risks (FINEX)Your Trusted Partner in Managing Complex Risk: Expertly navigating Litigation Risk, Cyber, Directors &amp; Officers, Financial Institutions, Mergers &amp