l Pan-Nox Emissions clients, so we should provide the ones for the other car manufacturers too (now, if easy to locate, or in the second tranche).&nbsp;Q17: the GLO. Mercedes GLO provided. Terms are broadly similar cross all the litigations. &nbsp; 17. GLO The SRA has asked for complete copies of the Pan-Nox GLOs, so we should provide the ones for the other car manufacturers too (now, if easy to locate, or in the second tranche)&nbsp;Regarding the additional documents scheduled for sharing tomorrow:&nbsp;Q3: &nbsp;Creditor action – the AP schedule will be ready early tomorrow morning. The timing for payments etc. will be captured within the excel schedule. We will also provide a short narrative for the letter. Q7: &nbsp;G3 funding documents – these can be shared. All relevant documents are contained in this folder &nbsp;7. G3 Funding Agreement and ancillary documentsQ8:&nbsp; Gramercy Influence - @Carolina Koschdoski de Souza will shortly provide a summary document to address this question. Once you've had a chance to review, we can decide whether to share this tomorrow or hold off until the second tranche. The question of Gramercy’s influence is a key question, and the answer understandably nuanced. I would like us properly to consider the draft response, including with input from Fergal who is flying today, and therefore propose that we hold off sending this until the second tranche. &nbsp;I am available early tomorrow morning until 10am if we need to catch up on anything but will be offline for the rest of the day. Carolina is on standby to assist with the letter finalisation /bundling the document pack. &nbsp;Kind regards Helena &nbsp;​​​​Helena&nbsp;YearwoodRisk&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Compliance&nbsp;DirectorFrom: Lawrence, Jonathan &lt;Jonathan.Lawrence@clydeco.com&gt; Sent: 22 October 2025 20:37To: Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Fergal Cathie &lt;Fergal.Cathie@clydeco.com&gt;; Rajwade, Maitreyi &lt;Maitreyi.Rajwade@clydeco.com&gt;; Alicia Al