itors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Lawrence, Jonathan &lt;Jonathan.Lawrence@clydeco.com&gt;Sent: Monday, October 20, 2025 9:12:23 AMTo: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Fergal Cathie &lt;Fergal.Cathie@clydeco.com&gt;; Rajwade, Maitreyi &lt;Maitreyi.Rajwade@clydeco.com&gt;Subject: Project Swift - call with Juliet Oliver - privileged [CC-UNITEDKINGDOM.145310.10756022] &nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Dear Alicia&nbsp;For information, Juliet Oliver of Stratify called me on Friday. &nbsp;Juliet asked if PG was going to be requesting an extension for the response to the SRA’s document request. I stated that it would not necessarily be doing so, and that PG would aim to comply with the deadline, but that it would not surprise Juliet if an extension might be required given the number of requests. Juliet stated that Gramercy was keen to pick up with PG in respect of anything that they could usefully contribute to the response, and that Juliet would make herself available for a call this week if helpful, though she is traveling in Hong Kong so we would need to work around the time differences. &nbsp;Juliet also stated that she understood that PG now has obtained the client file from Child &amp; Child. Juliet stated that within that file is a lot of paperwork that reveals what was passed on from Tom to the SRA. She reported that 