&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Raminder&nbsp;GrewalGlobal&nbsp;HR&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;718From: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Date: Wednesday, 1 October 2025 at 14:42To: Plate Litigation &lt;plate_litigation@pallasllp.com&gt;, Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Fw: The Case LeadsFYI - still finalising skel points but think we need to discuss this @Alicia Alinia&nbsp;in light of broader discussions with JLG etc - it's not clear how this would work and frankly the last bullet seems to suggest a narrower scope of work for that to be pressing at this stage - I assume this means the non-ALGLOs.​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From: Martyn Day &lt;mday@leighday.co.uk&gt;Sent: Wednesday, October 1, 2025 2:33 PMTo: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nichola Marshall &lt;nmarshall@leighday.co.uk&gt;Subject: The Case Leads &nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;&nbsp;Hi Anna/Alicia,&nbsp;Counsel have asked us whether we are able to say to the court, through them, that we are satisfied the PG Case Leads will remain involved in the case until the end of the year.Nic and I took the liberty to speak to them at lunchtime. They say they confirm they are happy to give that reassurance if the following conditions are met:-that a working agreement is put in place to be signed off by you and us applying to the five of them, ie Michael Burke, Priyanka Gladson, Matt Hunt, Georgie Fallows, and Sarah Bingham - not to the wider PG NOx team;that for the remainder of their tenure at PG, the five of them solely work on common cost matters across the Pan NOx Litigations;that they are not responsible for conducting PG only related work; that PG will update their various Claimant Committees that the case leads have stepped down and who the new case leads are within a reasonable time frame and in any event no more than 14 days;That all sounds reasonable, so can you confirm you are content with this so we can give the assurance to the court.Thanks&nbsp;Martyn&nbsp;Martyn&nbsp;Day​​​​Senior Partner020&nbsp;7650&nbsp;1200​leighday.co.ukFollow&nbsp;us&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Panagram, 27 Goswell Road, London, EC1M 7AJ&nbsp;We are committed to protecting your privacy when you use our services and treat all personal data in accordance with our Privacy Policy DisclaimerThe information contained in this communication from mday@leighday.co.uk sent at 2025-10-01 14:33:26 is confidential and may be legally privileged. It is intended solely for use by those authorised to receive it. If you are not so authorised, you are hereby notified that any disclosure, copying, distribution or taking action in reliance upon the contents of this information is strictly prohibited and may be unlawful. We do not accept service of documents by email. Please note that we only provide our bank account details in a password protected PDF. The password will be communicated separately by telephone. We will never send changes to our bank account details by email outside of this process. If you receive such an email, do not respond to it but contact us separately via your contact at the firm. Visit the Leigh Day website: https://www.leighday.co.uk Leigh Day is a partnership authorised and regulated by the Solicitors Regulation Authority (SRA). The firm's SRA number is 00067679. PLEASE THINK ABOUT THE ENVIRONMENT BEFORE PRINTING THIS EMAIL "}

