 on 20 August;Applications were made by the Defendants (without response to our 20 August letter) on 27 August;Witness evidence for the applications was filed 2 September;Skeletons were filed 8 SeptemberHearing 10 September and oral judgement handed down 11 September.&nbsp;&nbsp;The timeframe for these applications also overlapped with finalisation of the supplemental expert reports and the substantive PDD Trial skeleton. We have since been provided with cost schedules by the Defendants for us to consider them with the schedules still being updated even to date. The costs sought by the Defendants are as set out in the below table, with PG's proportionate share of those costs in red:&nbsp;ReportMercedes 29.84%Renault 44.42%Nissan 41.08%Ford 49.29%TotalHeitz£392,755.71 £117,198.30£124,867.13 £55,465.98£421,034.11&nbsp;£172,960.81£212,398.41 £104,691.18£1,151,055.36 £450,316.27Tate£70,543.30 £21,050.12£15,478.82 £6,875.69&nbsp;£24,947.94 £12,296.84£110,970.06&nbsp;£40,222.65Smithers&nbsp;£23,719.02 £10,535.99&nbsp;£31,421.72 £15,487.77£55,140.74 £26,023.76Glow Plugs&nbsp;£257,703.57 £114,471.92£315,388.56 £129,561.62&nbsp;£573,092.13 £244,033.54TOTAL£463,299.01&nbsp;£138,248.42£421,768.54 £187,349.58&nbsp;£736,422.67 £302,522.43£268,768.07 £132,475.79£1,890,258.29&nbsp;£&nbsp;On the issue of glow plugs, these were notified to the insurers on 18 August (per the attached). While not strictly for settlement at the PTR, the Renault and Nissan Defendants have made it clear that they need these costs to be considered as part of any deal they will do on the costs of the applications. We will attempt to resist this but it is prudent to seek approval now to allow us to negotiate.&nbsp;&nbsp;The Defendants have made it clear that should the parties be unable to reach an agreement, they will be seeking the Court make an order of indemnity costs against the Claimants at the PTR on Monday 6 October. The approach taken by so far has been to sound out the Defendants as to whether we can reach an agreement that avoids them making such an application. LD have sent a WP offer to Mercedes, &quot;offer[ing] either (i) 66% in relation to your clients’ statement of costs in respect of the Dr Heitz application, payable within 28 days, or (ii) an interim payment of your indemnity costs of 50% now, payable within 28 days, with the remainder to be assessed.&quot;&nbsp;We do not think this is something that will be acceptable across all of the Defendants, not least because there are nuances to how &quot;successful&quot; each Defendant was in their application.&nbsp;&nbsp;We would like to request authority to go to 80% of the due costs of the Heitz reports, 80% of the costs of the Smithers costs, 80% of the Glow Plugs costs, and for us to push the Tate costs to be Costs in the Case. This would equate to:&nbsp;ReportMercedesRenaultNissanFordTotalHeitz£93,758.64£44,372.78£138,368.65£83,752.94£360,253.01Tate&nbsp;Smithers&nbsp;£8,428.79&nbsp;£12,390.22£20,819.01Glow Plugs&nbsp;£91,577.54£103,649.30&nbsp;TOTAL£93,758.64£144,379.11£242,017.95£96,143.16£576,298.86&nbsp;If we can be of any further assistance, please let us know.&nbsp;&nbsp;Thanks,&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead&nbsp;From:&nbsp;James Burke &lt;james.burke2@wtwco.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Wednesday, October 01, 2025 6:28 PMTo:&nbsp;Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jonathan Simon &lt;Jonathan.Simon@wtwco.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Emissions Case Leads &lt;EmissionsCaseLeads@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Pan NOx Notification&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Hi Helena,&nbsp;Apologies for missing your calls, I was in a meeting this afternoon.&nbsp;For the moment insurers have reserved their rights in respect of any claim on the policy. They have also asked whether PG previously informed insurers about these applications and/or sought consent to contest them?&nbsp;Would you be able to give more information about the timing and making of the applications, the decision to contest them and their notice to insurers? I can see that there have been references to the expert reports in the periodic NOx updates but no express mention of the Defendants’ applications.&nbsp;The i.) Mercedes, and ii.) NOx wrapper policies have slightly different exclusion clauses in relation to adverse costs attributable to interim applications.&nbsp;The Mercedes policy excludes any claim under the policy attributable to “any interim application made or resisted without Insurer’s Approval” (clause 2.1.4).&nbsp;The NOx wrapper policies (Ford, RN and CP) excludes, unless Insurers Approval has been given, any claim under the policy attributable to:“The Insured’s intention to apply for summary judgment under CPR Part 24 or to make any other application which will be listed for or take half a day or more” (clause 4.1.4)&nbsp;The insurers have not yet sought to rely on these clauses but I would imagine these clauses are the context in which they seek further information. Given clause 4.1.4 above, it may also be that a notification was not required under the policy in any event.&nbsp;Regarding your instructions to Counsel – can you let us know the offer to settle the matters that you would like us to put to insurers for their agreement?&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;James Burke&nbsp;Associate Director (Solicitor)Litigation and Contingent Risk FINEX Global&nbsp;WTWOn behalf of Willis Limited, 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ (registered number 181116)On behalf of Willis Towers Watson SA/NV, Quai des Vennes, 4020, Liège, Belgium (registered as a branch in the UK at 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ UK Branch Number BR021056) in relation to all EEA-regulated business&nbsp;D: +44 (0)20 31248037M: +44 (0)7831 162591&nbsp;james.burke2@wtwco.comwww.wtwco.com&nbsp;Financial, Professional, and Executive Risks (FINEX)Your Trust