eesYour client would be expected to reconfirm his commitment to comply in full with the non-solicitation of employees clause at Clause 22.2(c) (corrected cross reference from our original letter) of his Service Agreement save that the obligation would be extended to cover both Key Employees (as defined) and all other fee earners (qualified solicitors, barristers and paralegals) at Pogust Goodhead;&nbsp;Update: We did discuss a list of Key Employees/employees PG would want covered. Although this is a good idea – it will be easier to agree a blanket ban otherwise there could be haggling over particular employees/ levels of employee particularly in the time available They might push back on the other fee earners saying that is not in his contract. “Key Employee” only includes those with supervisory or strategic responsibility for Group Litigation only.Alternatively they might say that they will accept the additional restriction for consideration. They could also seek to accept the wider covenant for a reduced period.7.Non dealing with clientsYour client would be expected to reconfirm his commitment to comply in full with the non-dealing with clients’ clause at Clause 22.4 of his Service Agreement, and the definition of Key Clients shall be amended to make clear that this comprises Pogust Goodhead’s 750,000 NOx emission clients;&nbsp;Update: to include without limitation – each PG manufacturer claimant committee. The definition of Key Client excludes clients with whom he dealt on a minimal basis – which presumably could be all of the Nox emission clients. It is possible that they would be caught by the limb re Confidential Information but ideally we would extend this as requested Alternatively they might say that they will accept the additional restriction for consideration. They could also seek to accept the wider covenant for a reduced period.8.Non solicitation of clients and client committeeYour client would be expected to agree to a provision regarding the non-solicitation of clients’ for 12 months post theTermination Date, which will cover both the direct solicitation of Pogust Goodhead’s750,000 NOx emission clients but also indirect solicitation of those clients via the claimant client committee for the NOx emission litigation;&nbsp;Update: to include without limitation – each PG manufacturer claimant committee.There is no non solicitation of clients clause in his contract of employmentThey may argue that if he agrees to the non dealing clause why do we also need a non solicitation clause – the answer is because he could solicit the clients via the client committee and then others could deal with themThey might say that they will only accept the additional restriction for consideration.They could also seek to accept the wider covenant for a reduced period.9.New employer covenantsOur client would expect your client’s new employer to also enter into 12 month non solicitation and non dealing restrictive covenants from the Termination Date that it will not:-solicit or deal with Pogust Goodhead’s NOx emission clients subject to the standard de-duplication processes that have already been agreed in respect of clients generally.solicit Pogust Goodhead’s NOx emission clients via each PG manufacturer claimant committeeneither employ nor make any offer of employment to any fee earners (qualified solicitors, barristers and paralegals) at Pogust Goodhead; andnot attempt to join any Steering Committee or become a Lead Solicitor in the NOx litigation for as long as your client is employed by the new employer.&nbsp;&nbsp;Given that we don’t trust Gallagher we need his new employer to give us some comfort10.ConfidentialityYour client would be expected to agree to comprehensive confidentiality provisions save that it would be accepted that your client could work as part of the broader claimant cohort as part of the ongoing NOx emissions matter;&nbsp;Update: The carve out is to be linked to the CRO. It is agreed that information or documents 